{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Target\n`src/rebar/_commands/init.py` — **786 LOC** on origin/main (re-measured at `059d54b725`) against\nthe 800-LOC hard cap: 14 lines of headroom.\n\n## The concern boundary (derived from the call graph)\n\n`init.py` today carries TWO subsystems with different owners, different lifecycles and no calls\nbetween them:\n\n1. **Host-repo tracker provisioning** (the `init` command proper) — resolve the repo, write\n   `.git/info/exclude`, take the 30s mkdir lock, mount-or-create the `tickets` branch worktree,\n   the linked-worktree symlink path, the `pending_init_*` predicates, and the CLI entry point.\n   Entry points: `init_cli` → `init_core` → `_mount_or_create_branch` / `_init_via_symlink`.\n\n2. **Tickets-branch convergence units** — the check-then-act, idempotent, drift-correcting\n   ensure units. `init.py` does **not** call these. Their sole caller is\n   `rebar._store.ensures._registry()`, which lazy-imports them by name and dispatches them from\n   `run_ensures()`. `ensures.py`'s own module docstring already records the seam verbatim: *\"The\n   unit implementations live in `rebar._commands.init` (they own the `.gitignore`/\n   `.gitattributes` content constants); `run_ensures` lazy-imports them.\"* That sentence IS the\n   architectural boundary — the units live in `init.py` only because they own the two content\n   templates, not because init calls them.\n\nThe split follows seam 2: extract the **content/config convergence units together with the two\ncontent templates they are the sole readers of**.\n\n## What moves — `src/rebar/_commands/_init_ensures.py` (new, ~215 LOC)\n- `_GITIGNORE`, `_GITATTRIBUTES` (the tickets-branch content templates)\n- `_gc_config_unit`, `_merge_ours_unit` (git-config convergence)\n- `_gitignore_unit`, `_gitattributes_unit`, `_store_compat_unit` (committed-blob convergence)\n- a module-local `_git` thin wrapper over the shared `rebar._store.gitutil.run_git_write` seam\n  (same two-line form init keeps, carrying its `# raw-git-ok:` marker)\n\n## What deliberately STAYS in `init.py` (~600 LOC), and why\n- Everything in subsystem 1.\n- `_untrack_runtime_markers_unit` + `_UNTRACK_BATCH`. Two reasons: (a) it is not a *content*\n  converger — it has no template and repairs a legacy INDEX state (`git rm --cached`) rather\n  than materializing a tickets-branch artifact; (b) **binding**:\n  `tests/unit/test_ensures_untrack_markers.py:155` does\n  `monkeypatch.setattr(init_mod, \"_UNTRACK_BATCH\", 3)` and then calls the unit. Moving the unit\n  away from the constant would silently stop that patch applying — the test would still pass\n  while no longer exercising the multi-batch path. That is a behaviour change, so the unit stays\n  with the constant it reads.\n\n## Binding check — BOTH sides, already performed\nSerena `find_referencing_symbols` + a plain string `grep` for every moved symbol across\n`src/ tests/ docs/ scripts/ .github/`. Findings that constrain the seam:\n- `src/rebar/_store/ensures.py:96-100` reaches the units as **module attributes**\n  (`init._gc_config_unit`, …). Preserved by re-exporting the moved names from `init.py`, so\n  `_registry()` needs no change and `test_ensures_untrack_markers.py:214`'s\n  `is`-identity assertion keeps holding.\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_ensure_drift_matrix.py:25` does\n  `from rebar._commands.init import _GITIGNORE` — preserved by the same re-export.\n- Monkeypatches pinned to the `init` module (`run_git`, `_git`, `_git_ok`, `_git_fetch`,\n  `_ensure_branch_user_config`, `init_core`, `_UNTRACK_BATCH`) all target symbols that STAY;\n  verified that no test patches `init._git` on any path that reaches a moved unit\n  (`tests/interfaces/store/test_ensures.py` and `test_ensure_drift_matrix.py` patch only env\n  vars, `ensures.write_lock` and `ensures._registry`).\n- Prose citations naming `init._gc_config_unit` / `_gitignore_unit` / `_store_compat_unit`\n  (`_store/sync.py`, `_store/project_ensures.py`, `docs/adr/0051`, `docs/scale-envelope.md`,\n  `docs/migrations.md`, two test docstrings) stay TRUE because of the re-export; the one\n  sentence that names the units' *home* — `ensures.py`'s module docstring — is updated to name\n  the new module.\n\n## Path-keyed registries checked (lesson from Gerrit 1916)\n- `.github/complexity-baseline.json` — keyed `<path>::<symbol>`; the only `init.py` entry is\n  `_mount_or_create_branch` (18), which STAYS, so the move adds no key. Verified by running\n  `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` directly and requiring\n  `new=0 increased=0 stale=0`.\n- `tests/scripts/test_cli_seam_clean_heldout.py` `_OWNED_FILES` / `_MARKER_BUDGET` — the new\n  module carries zero ambient config reads and zero `# read-via:` markers, so the\n  config-ownership gate stays at zero findings for the owned set.\n- `scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py` — the moved `_git` wrapper carries its `# raw-git-ok:`\n  reason marker so the raw-git gate stays green.\n- `tests/unit/test_init_no_hardcoded_tracker.py` scans `init_mod.__file__`; the moved text\n  contains no single-line `.tickets-tracker` literal, so its guarded surface is unchanged.\n- `.github/module-size-limit.txt` is NOT touched.\n\n## Method\nBehaviour-preserving move only — no logic edits. RED first: a size assertion demonstrating\n`init.py` over the target, plus running the existing ensure suites against the new layout;\nGREEN by the move. No existing test is modified.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_commands/init.py` is at or below 650 LOC (real headroom, well inside the\n      gate's `LIMIT - LIMIT/10` = 720 near-cap band), and `_init_ensures.py` is >= 100 LOC.\n- [ ] The five moved units and the two content templates live in `_init_ensures.py`; `init.py`\n      re-exports them so `ensures._registry()` and every `init._<name>` citation still resolve.\n- [ ] Behaviour unchanged: `tests/unit/test_ensures_untrack_markers.py`,\n      `tests/interfaces/store/test_ensures.py`, `tests/interfaces/store/test_ensure_drift_matrix.py`,\n      `tests/unit/test_init_attach_predicate.py`, `tests/unit/test_git_timeout_bounds_983f.py`,\n      `tests/unit/test_init_no_hardcoded_tracker.py` and\n      `tests/scripts/test_cli_seam_clean_heldout.py` all pass UNMODIFIED.\n- [ ] The whole non-integration/non-external suite passes — validated across the WHOLE tree\n      (`tests/unit`, `tests/interfaces`, `tests/scripts`, `tests/e2e`), not one directory.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass, and `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py\n      --check` reports `new=0 increased=0 stale=0`.\n- [ ] `.github/module-size-limit.txt` is byte-identical to origin/main.\n- [ ] The commit message NAMES the concern boundary and says why the call graph supports it."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787190119994509001,"uuid":"142b6ce4-eac1-4b59-bb2a-731db0b6f4db"}